Queue::checkError's report in the release build.

The release build compiles DK_WARNING out, so a queue's entry into its error
state (a GPU page fault with its address and access, a method error, a
rejected command list, a timeout) left nothing behind but the abort at the
next submission ("attempt to submit commands to a queue in error state",
2359-0001). In the release build the warnings in gpu_error.cpp go to a weak
dkErrorReport(fmt, ...) when the program defines one.

diff --git a/source/gpu_error.cpp b/source/gpu_error.cpp
index 5e9dd7e..eecfd27 100644
--- a/source/gpu_error.cpp
+++ b/source/gpu_error.cpp
@@ -3,6 +3,16 @@
 
 using namespace dk::detail;
 
+#ifndef DEBUG
+// The release build's warnings are compiled out, which leaves a queue's error
+// (a GPU page fault and its address, a method error, a timeout) unsaid before
+// the next submission aborts: they go to the program's dkErrorReport, if it
+// defines one.
+extern "C" void dkErrorReport(const char* fmt, ...) __attribute__((weak, format(printf, 1, 2)));
+#undef DK_WARNING
+#define DK_WARNING(...) do { if (dkErrorReport) dkErrorReport(__VA_ARGS__); } while (0)
+#endif
+
 void Device::checkQueueErrors() noexcept
 {
 	MutexHolder m{m_queueTableMutex};
